  "notes": [
    "Both versions ran in the same disposable synthetic-only Zotero 10.0.4 profile using 480 unique five-page image/vector PDFs and a 97-page, 76.98 MB PDF.",
    "Each benchmark started with an empty thumbnail directory. Requested concurrency 3 has no effect in the 0.1.8 baseline.",
    "The baseline native observer confirmed decoded-surface discards under memory pressure and 8 new image loads on scrollback despite 0 thumbnail-engine reads/renders.",
    "The final run reused the exact image node, produced pixel-identical canvas output after memory pressure, and had 0 new image loads, JS decode calls, native frame/decode events, or thumbnail-engine reads/renders on scrollback.",
    "All 480 retained native image locks were released on controller destruction. The 480-preview working set fits within the 512 MiB decoded-pixel cap; this test does not claim that all 2000 maximum-size previews stay decoded simultaneously.",
    "Times are single local synthetic runs, not broad benchmark estimates. Scroll traversal includes deliberate 25 ms readiness polling and is not used as a raw throughput metric.",
    "Headless Zotero logs a software compositor framebuffer warning; the final run independently draws the retained image to canvas and verifies the complete pixel checksum."
